{"data": [{"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:33:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112885030934413813"], "id": "2112885030934413813", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1134520615241543680", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112884767704469519", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@alexlikesgtrs @ZenithcoreAi Grok Bot is real. It gives always-on agents their own cloud computer that can research niches via X/web, build and publish pages, handle email inboxes, run scheduled routines, and work while your laptop is closed. Users do set up directory-style sites and affiliate flows this", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2112885030934413813"}, {"author_id": "233042694", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:32:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112884678927831494"], "id": "2112884678927831494", "in_reply_to_user_id": "233042694", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112884622665412681", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "It looks like the computer's built-in login sharing copies browser logins into every bot's Chrome. How can I keep each bot's browser logins separate? Is there a setting to turn off login sharing for each bot, or is a separate Grok Bot account per brand the only way?", "url": "https://x.com/megavinvin93/status/2112884678927831494"}, {"author_id": "14550264", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:28:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112883798085873919"], "id": "2112883798085873919", "in_reply_to_user_id": "120470965", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112883200435368194", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@iammarcthomas ok, heres the use case that inspired the set up!\n\nI was evaluating some email verification tools, they all have like free sample pages when you can eval one email at a time\n\nSo I wanted to put in 10 emails that we knew some were good and some bounced and see what each tool came", "url": "https://x.com/lkr/status/2112883798085873919"}, {"author_id": "2014893755078475776", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:28:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112883789177483278"], "id": "2112883789177483278", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2832427459", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112246281016119780", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@poteto @bot This week my GrokBot :\n\n🌴 Built out 3 full websites\n🌐 Registered and paid for two new domains for upcoming sites by itself\n🎬 Made first YouTube Short from scratch: script, voiceover, sound effects, all coded, for barely 2% of weekly usage\n+ much more", "url": "https://x.com/ProtonJan/status/2112883789177483278"}, {"article": {"title": "What the Fastest-Growing AI Companies Are Teaching Founders About Building in 2026"}, "author_id": "3310065154", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:25:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112882855571574997"], "id": "2112882855571574997", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Some of the fastest-growing AI companies right now are growing for very different reasons.\n\nThey’re getting really good at owning a specific job, fitting into real workflows, &amp; adapting as the market changes.\n\nRead the full blog: https://t.co/mh4KrRg4Hy", "url": "https://x.com/sudiptabiswas93/status/2112882855571574997"}, {"article": {"title": "My Grok Bot Team Finds the Deals. I Make Every Call."}, "author_id": "3158984637", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:23:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112882533251834320"], "id": "2112882533251834320", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "For three days straight my deal bot found nothing, and I thanked God for it. That empty report taught me more about investing than any full one. https://t.co/F6xr0Ttyyq", "url": "https://x.com/zaneccampbell/status/2112882533251834320"}, {"article": {"title": "合上电脑还在替你干活：Grok Bot 低成本白嫖、录屏调教与防翻车实操指南（附 Muse / Dots 横评）"}, "author_id": "2060554585643843585", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:19:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112881501310443565"], "id": "2112881501310443565", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "合上电脑还在替你干活：Grok Bot 低成本白嫖、录屏调教与防翻车实操指南（附 Muse / Dots 横评） https://t.co/9e2t3KpBln", "url": "https://x.com/cyberde05/status/2112881501310443565"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2112865688519880704"]}, "author_id": "4633060354", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:19:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112881493575917921"], "id": "2112881493575917921", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2093607787817267607", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "SpaceXAI's Grok Bot team put 10 of its own bot templates in the marketplace, and this is a f*c*ing goldmine\n\nyou don't write a system prompt from scratch, you import a setup built for one job, connect your tools, and adapt it\n\nthe 10:\n\n1. dr eggbot builds other Grok Bots. https://t.co/QbY6KUPPpA https://t.co/sUArO9KSS9", "url": "https://x.com/hammertime_one/status/2112881493575917921"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2112878509739708416"]}, "author_id": "6452362", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:15:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112878934505267669", "2112880538516124002"], "id": "2112880538516124002", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 73, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Made the second music video with the Grok Bot Video Studio I built and this one has a pretty interesting backstory. Way back in late February I was working with my first Autonomous AI agent @aionaedge at the time an OpenClaw Foundation AI. Among the nightly research that Aiona https://t.co/0Ik61JJvnt", "url": "https://x.com/MichaelGannotti/status/2112880538516124002"}, {"article": {"title": "Written in the Stars: Tell Me a Story"}, "author_id": "2096298388752863237", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:15:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112880448724414541"], "id": "2112880448724414541", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 78, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/7SSxkGo2Gl", "url": "https://x.com/constellatio42/status/2112880448724414541"}, {"author_id": "1766658206023946240", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:12:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112879731292942543"], "id": "2112879731292942543", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Whether you build with Grok Bot or OpenAI's Dots, two things matter most.\n\n1. Every new project needs a code map and a dev collaboration workflow. It should spell out:\n- How humans and agents work together: when to hand work to the agent, and what it's responsible for.\n- How the", "url": "https://x.com/techcatboss/status/2112879731292942543"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2112878509739708416"]}, "author_id": "6452362", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:09:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112878934505267669", "2112880538516124002"], "id": "2112878934505267669", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 60, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Made the second music video with the Grok Bot Video Studio I built and this one has a pretty interesting backstory. Way back in late February I was working with my first Autonomous AI agent @aionaedge at the time an OpenClaw Foundation AI. Among the nightly research that Aiona https://t.co/y3FKYqTYZr", "url": "https://x.com/MichaelGannotti/status/2112878934505267669"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2112878678648434688"]}, "author_id": "1918346924463202304", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:08:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112878801633861648"], "id": "2112878801633861648", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 25, "impression_count": 467, "like_count": 33, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2109235458383216811", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "grok bot routines will quietly eat your budget if you set them and forget them\n\nsame bot. same job. 12x the cost.\n\na watcher firing every 5 minutes wakes up 8,640 times a month. at grok 4.6 api rates that's around $397. the hourly version sits near $33\n\nhow to stop the bleed: https://t.co/sCwlZoGF2j https://t.co/fPYrAvf9Sp", "url": "https://x.com/gippp69/status/2112878801633861648"}, {"author_id": "1537305472478453767", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:06:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112878121850450037"], "id": "2112878121850450037", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2048564521631916032", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112857193615884785", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ConnorTalksAI Muse and Dots have their use and strengths, but Grok Bot is by far the easiest to set up and organize teams of specialized bots - much like you would have employees in a startup.", "url": "https://x.com/KenTaylorBuilds/status/2112878121850450037"}, {"author_id": "1013749216387256322", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:02:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112877144032657421"], "id": "2112877144032657421", "in_reply_to_user_id": "10307712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112568859266035779", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@stalman Don't switch... atleast not Fully\nKeep atleast 20$ worth codex for your regular tasks\nGet the 20/30$ grok bot - it'll have decent usage for research, automated tasks, etc. \nBut the usage limits on Grok are too low if you want to work on a decently big project", "url": "https://x.com/aakashbuildsAI/status/2112877144032657421"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112876972779171840"]}, "author_id": "1464473168811544576", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:01:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112877017737974007"], "id": "2112877017737974007", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112791586283340250", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "刚接触 Grok Bot，最容易的坑是一上来就搭 20 个 Bot。\n\n我第一周只钉了两件事：下午日更一条 Routine、晚上复盘一条 Routine。先跑通「它自己醒 → 写文件 → 我只看结果」，再谈多 Bot 协作。\n\n@cgnot996 这篇四步路线很适合当目录。你第一周先跑通了哪一步？ https://t.co/Ylh8mF4zzC https://t.co/EaE3cI8AYk", "url": "https://x.com/TodayKan/status/2112877017737974007"}, {"author_id": "3014436799", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:01:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112876983222685977"], "id": "2112876983222685977", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1948016777067216896", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112717140231119356", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Wade_Texas @awayslice Over 560 at rest API’s so you can bit bang with the Ai of your choice. \n\nGrok Bot and terminal AI’s do a phenomenal job - require dry run verification and all entries are entered as ‘system’ for human validation. \n\nSlowBooks Pro is purpose built for Ai.", "url": "https://x.com/SlowBooksPro/status/2112876983222685977"}, {"author_id": "2085838061347217408", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:01:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112876944135970958"], "id": "2112876944135970958", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2112575839485501441", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 48, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112876894781886749", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@buminduYR @poteto Sending that to your Grok Bot now. It’ll handle the full breakdown and workflow ideas for you.", "url": "https://x.com/bot/status/2112876944135970958"}, {"article": {"title": "Hand real work to AI by giving every bot one job: the four-bot team that runs my X account"}, "author_id": "1644401923787726849", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:01:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112876834182541338"], "id": "2112876834182541338", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 282, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/kVbAYRkR9g", "url": "https://x.com/Zephyr_hg/status/2112876834182541338"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["7_2112876791492661248"]}, "author_id": "873738597731631104", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:01:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112876808131449222"], "id": "2112876808131449222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "I've not abandoned my love for retro tech! I'm learning how to make things fancier and shinier to show off more retro machines. This is my very first draft; a 3D model that my Grok @Bot built in Blender, spinning inside a trading card!\n\nIt's a bit rough, I'm still figuring out https://t.co/qPRePm44xN", "url": "https://x.com/tommithetechie/status/2112876808131449222"}, {"author_id": "101584084", "created_at": "2026-10-21T12:00:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112876706377990160"], "id": "2112876706377990160", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1534669402012061697", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 206, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112870660129116297", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Markymark1025 Grok Bot’s X Money routine builds a Monday dashboard from the account itself: balance changes, auto-categorized transactions with week-over-week trends, cash-back and interest totals, flagged subscriptions, habit tips drawn from the numbers, and progress rings for savings rate,", "url": "https://x.com/BrianRoemmele/status/2112876706377990160"}, {"article": {"title": "Agents shouldn't live on your laptop anymore"}, "author_id": "2076612813557059584", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:59:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112876529000534036"], "id": "2112876529000534036", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 76, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"running a terminal on your phone sounds awful. who would want to work that way? moshi shows it works, and does it really well\" - new drop by @sulich_olaf with a free agent skill for setting up a remote agent host\n\nget your freebie inside 👇 https://t.co/HoDMwCc1Fq", "url": "https://x.com/megadevhq/status/2112876529000534036"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2112875063212933121"]}, "author_id": "1654574824348368897", "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:54:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112875260060299296"], "id": "2112875260060299296", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Same game idea, two AI builders.\n\nLeft: Sky Rumble, built by my @bot (Grokbot).\n\nRight: Sky Rogue, built with @spawn.\n\nWhich one do you like more? https://t.co/UTEuFthW